**Before the Trinity launch (the rehearsal included), each with a test, then re-pin and send me the digest:**

1. **F1 (medium; `chain_save.py:76-85`, `execute_chain.py:136-138`)**: the archive output folder is never refused when it is on `/home` or `/data*`. Pointed there, the read would write an unthrottled archive every 120 seconds onto network storage. Run the output path through `common.local`, or require `/scratch` when the site is Trinity.
